<title>FRANCE: French May industrial production drops 1.6 pct.</title>
<headline>French May industrial production drops 1.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE said industrial production, excluding construction, fell 1.6 percent in May from the previous month and was up 2.2 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Industrial production excluding energy, agri-food businesses and construction -- considered by INSEE the best measure of manufacturing output -- fell 1.7 percent in May from the previous month, giving a year-on-year rise of 3.1 percent.  </p>
<p>INSEE gave the following seasonally adjusted percentage changes:</p>
<p>					May vs Apr  Apr vs Mar  May yr/yr*</p>
<p> Industrial production index     -1.6	  3.1	   2.2</p>
<p> Manufacturing output		-1.7	  1.1	   3.1</p>
<p> Agri-food			     -2.0	  3.6	   3.3</p>
<p> Consumer goods			-1.0	  2.9	   1.3</p>
<p> Car industry			  -3.2	  3.5	   2.9</p>
<p> Industrial capital goods	  -1.2	  0.9	   1.7</p>
<p> Semi-finished goods		 -1.7	  0.1	   4.6</p>
<p> Energy				  -1.4	 14.7	  -3.6</p>
<p> Construction			  -0.3	 -2.3	  -1.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Comparison with year-ago period is for three months to end May versus the three months in the same period last year.  </p>
<p>The data is based on a new index introduced in January 1996.</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following seasonally adjusted data for industrial production indices.</p>
<p>							May  April   March</p>
<p> Industrial production index		101.8  103.5   100.4</p>
<p> Manufacturing output			  98.0   99.7    98.6</p>
<p>  Agri-food				     112.1  114.4   110.4</p>
<p>  Energy					  117.6  119.3   104.0</p>
<p>  Semi-finished goods			 102.9  104.7   104.6</p>
<p>  Industrial capital goods		   87.3   88.4    87.6</p>
<p>  Car industry				  105.1  108.6   104.9</p>
<p>  Consumer goods				 98.7   99.7    96.9</p>
<p>  Construction				   89.0   89.3    91.4</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom + 33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
